[Music]  the coronavirus crisis is having a  dramatic impact on us we have lost so  far tens of thousands of people in the  European Union to this virus our health  care systems aren't an enormous strain  and our economy is severely hit many  people fear for their lives and also for  their jobs defeating this virus requires  unprecedented measures even before the  first cases were reported in the  European Union we took steps to prepare  for this disease  [Music]  [Music]  soon we also started to help bring back  European citizens stranded across the  world  [Music]  at the same time we swiftly mobilized  funding for research because we need  vaccines new treatments and better  diagnosis methods to fight this virus  [Music]  the dramatic outbreak in Wuhan made us  quickly recognize its serious risks to  public health worldwide one of our first  priorities was therefore calling out to  member states to raise their  preparedness coordinate on all levels  and demonstrate international solidarity  firstly toward China as well as among  each other  [Music]  as the virus spread rapidly throughout  the European Union we stepped up our  response on all fronts medical economic  mobility Civil Protection and many more  [Music]  we need the best scientific evidence to  fight this virus and this is why I  gathered a team of leading European  experts to advise us  we could step to help ensure that our  hospitals have the equipment they need  the Commission has been working with  industry to ramp up production of  protective and medical equipment such as  ventilators and it is helping member  states buy equipment through joint  procurement  member states first reaction was to  impose border controls these led to  significant waiting times at some border  crossings of more than 24 hours we have  worked intensively with national  governments to overcome the blockage and  the lace we acted fast to unblock  traffic to enable people to reach their  homes or workplaces and to make sure  that goods could be delivered where they  were needed from hospitals to shops  [Music]  and because the containment measures hit  the economy we have unlocked funding to  fight the crisis we provided billions of  euros in support from the EU budget and  we adapted the rules to enable  governments to pump money in the economy  to protect people's jobs and to keep  businesses running support measures are  more than three trillion euros have been  announced so far in the European Union  this is the most impressive response  anywhere in the world  [Music]  in parallel we are working with our  international partners on a coordinated  global response that's the only way to  beat the virus  we have made real progress by working  closely together in the EU against the  coronavirus the spread of the virus has  started to slow down now we are working  with governments to help ensure a  gradual and coordinated lifting of  containment measures when the right time  comes  [Music]  we are also working on a robust recovery  plan to kick-start our economy and  create jobs for Europeans and to make  Europe stronger and more resilient

